.anti-legacy | Anti-legacy review of designs against flagged patterns | architecture-governance | E\n19\t   ARCH.GOV.radar | Technology radar & maturity tiers with promotion criteria | architecture-governance | E\n20\t   ARCH.GOV.coding-standard | Coding standard & language subset | architecture-governance | E\n21\t # ARCH.EVID Research & evidence\n22\t   ARCH.EVID.grading | Source grading & provenance tiers | research-evidence | E\n23\t   ARCH.EVID.survey | Literature survey protocol per decision | research-evidence | E\n24\t   ARCH.EVID.spike | Prototype/spike protocol producing evidence where literature is thin | research-evidence | E\n25\t   ARCH.EVID.claims | Benchmark-backed claims standard | research-evidence | E\n26\t # ARCH.ORG Agent organization\n27\t   ARCH.ORG.decomposition | Milestone → task decomposition by skill territory | program-orchestration | E\n28\t   ARCH.ORG.ownership-ledger | Ownership ledger & territory locks | program-orchestration | E\n29\t   ARCH.ORG.integration | Integration sequencing & milestone vertical slices | program-orchestration | E\n30\t   ARCH.ORG.change-requests | Contract change-request protocol between agents | program-orchestration | E\n31\t   ARCH.ORG.critic-gates | Scheduling critic gates per stage | program-orchestration | E\n32\t## PLAT Platform & hardware abstraction\n33\t # PLAT.PAL Platform abstraction layer\n34\t   PLAT.PAL.os | OS services abstraction (threads, virtual memory, files, time, dynamic libraries) | platform-architect | E\n35\t   PLAT.PAL.cpu-topology | CPU topology & feature discovery (hybrid cores, SMT, caches, NUMA, ISA) | platform-architect | E\n36\t   PLAT.PAL.windowing | Windowing & surfaces | platform-architect | E\n37\t   PLAT.PAL.lifecycle | Process lifecycle (suspend, resume, constrained, terminate) | platform-architect | E\n38\t   PLAT.PAL.capability-tiers | Platform capability tiers & feature query | platform-architect | E\n39\t   PLAT.PAL.web | Web target (WASM + WebGPU) | platform-architect