{"parentUuid":"f10ccfc6-b2ad-4336-a052-1d8eee374430","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"aa9944ad1d1eb99b1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TSZd8TFwNs6jVVSdH23drP","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/06-gap-analysis.md-59-These are admitted limits of phase 1 that critics should keep testing:\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md-60-\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md-61-1. **Parameters behind NDAs.** Console-specific skills can be *structured* now but not *filled*. Phase 2 must mark console content as \"requires licensed platform documentation\".\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:62:2. **Game-specific systems.** Game-specific systems (inventory, quests, dialogue trees, economy) are treated as game code on top of `C-GAME`, not engine capabilities. This boundary is deliberate and may be challenged per genre.\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md-63-3. **Backend services.** Backend services are outside engine scope by decision (`engine-architect` non-goal register). The engine owns only the integration boundary.\n101 docs/00-design-principles.md\ninfo: 739 capabilities, 124 skills, 62 contracts, 14 critics\nWARN: expert skill plugin-system owns only 2 capabilities (microscopic?)\nWARN: expert skill asset-cook-processors owns only 2 capabilities (microscopic?)\n\n0 errors, 2 warnings","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f5e42b33-70dc-4aad-8a1c-40686821edf2","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:49:39.209Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f10ccfc6-b2ad-4336-a052-1d8eee374430","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
