{"parentUuid":"c6e5a58b-b6f2-43a3-9475-d47d3a0ce5fe","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa9944ad1d1eb99b1","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfXzgdDJdfgwW1if9rGfb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TKakzDGB6cGh5AZNWPuY13","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework && python3 -c \"\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('data/skills.json'))\nprint(s.keys())\nsk=s['skills'] if 'skills' in s else s\nfor k in sk[:1]: print(k)\n\" ; python3 -c \"\nimport json,re\ns=json.load(open('data/skills.json'))['skills']\nfor k in s:\n  p=k.get('purpose','')\n  if re.search(r'tool|editor|author',p,re.I): print(k['id'],'::',p[:220])\n\"","description":"Find skills whose purpose mentions tools/authoring"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4415,"cache_read_input_tokens":96756,"output_tokens":2108,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1840},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4415},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2108,"cache_read_input_tokens":96756,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4415,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TKakzDGB6cGh5AZNWPuY13":{"command":"cd /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework && python3 -c \"\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('data/skills.json'))\nprint(s.keys())\nsk=s['skills'] if 'skills' in s else s\nfor k in sk[:1]: print(k)\n\" ; python3 -c \"\nimport json,re\ns=json.load(open('data/skills.json'))['skills']\nfor k in s:\n  p=k.get('purpose','')\n  if re.search(r'tool|editor|author',p,re.I): print(k['id'],'::',p[:220])\n\"","description":"Find skills whose purpose mentions tools/authoring"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfXzgcvTAgbKFCav4n2X9","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"191240bb-daa2-4fe5-be59-85dcd3d81293","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:50:03.893Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
{"parentUuid":"191240bb-daa2-4fe5-be59-85dcd3d81293","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"aa9944ad1d1eb99b1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TKakzDGB6cGh5AZNWPuY13","type":"tool_result","content":"dict_keys(['_doc', 'profiles', 'configurations', 'skills'])\n{'id': 'engine-architect', 'name': 'Game Engine Chief Architect', 'tier': 'orchestrator', 'parent': None, 'profiles': ['all'], 'runtime': False, 'purpose': \"Owns the engine's overall architecture: requirements and configuration profiles, layering and module boundaries, the contract registry, global conventions, build/integrate/buy decisions and cross-domain arbitration. Final authority on the boundaries between skills.\", 'non_responsibilities': [['Running the ADR, fitness-function and anti-legacy process', 'architecture-governance'], ['Scheduling work across agents and the ownership ledger', 'program-orchestration'], ['Architecture inside a domain (e.g. shading-path choice)', 'render-architect']], 'provides': ['C-ARCH'], 'consumes': [], 'expertise': ['engine architecture', 'requirements engineering', 'trade-off analysis', 'architecture views']}\nengine-architect :: Owns the engine's overall architecture: requirements and configuration profiles, layering and module boundaries, the contract registry, global conventions, build/integrate/buy decisions and cross-domain arbitration. Fina\nresearch-evidence :: Research discipline for every major decision: finds and grades authoritative evidence (production talks, platform docs, peer-reviewed work, reproducible benchmarks), classifies techniques as established / emerging / expe\ngpu-performance :: GPU performance analysis and review: occupancy, bandwidth, cache behavior, barrier and async-compute overlap, vendor tools across PC, console and mobile, GPU power.\nanti-cheat-integrity :: Cheat resistance for online games: server-authoritative validation patterns (movement, hits, economy), rate limiting, anomaly signals, integration boundary for client anti-cheat middleware.\napi-lifecycle-migration :: Public API surface, semantic versioning and deprecation, ABI policy, engine-upgrade tooling (codemods, data upgraders) and LTS policy, so projects can move across engine versions.\necs-runtime :: ECS: storage (archetype chunks or sparse sets, chosen by ADR), queries, change detection, structural changes and command buffers, system scheduling with access-conflict analysis, relationships, singletons, authoring → ru\nreflection-metadata :: Type registry, reflection generation (codegen now, C++26 static reflection when toolchains allow), attributes, the property system, script-binding substrate, dynamic invocation.\nterrain :: Terrain end-to-end: representation, rendering, material layering, sculpt/paint tool logic, runtime deformation, collision data hand-off.\nprocedural-generation :: Deterministic graph-based PCG framework usable in editor and at stream-in, placement and scattering rules, grammar and constraint methods; evaluates ML generation.\nshader-system :: Shading language and dialect, compilation toolchain, permutations, reflection and binding layouts, interop headers, caches and distributed compilation, hot reload, shader debugging, PSO-list gathering.\ndestruction-fracture :: Fracture authoring and precomputation, runtime fracture and debris, destruction replication strategy, propagation to navigation, rendering and audio.\naudio-content-runtime :: Audio event system and parameters, interactive music, dialogue and VO, authoring tool integration, audio-to-haptics.\nnetwork-architect :: Netcode model per game type (authoritative server, lockstep, rollback, P2P/relay), network tick and time, authority model, budgets and scale targets, protocol versioning, sharded worlds evaluation.\nui-architect :: UI architecture (retained with data binding for game UI, immediate for developer UI), layout, styling, focus and navigation, animation, in-world UI, designer tool logic, UI performance.\neditor-architect :: Editor architecture: process model (in- vs out-of-process runtime), editor/runtime data separation, transactions and undo/redo, selection, extension API and tool scripting, play-in-editor isolation, remote live editing, \neditor-ui-framework :: Tool UI toolkit (docking, panels), reflection-driven inspectors, asset browser, immediate-mode developer UI, editor UX standards.\nworld-editor-viewport :: Viewport and navigation, gizmos, snapping and placement, partition-aware world editing, spline tools, environment tool-mode hosting.\ngraph-editor-framework :: Shared node-graph editor for material, animation, VFX, audio, PCG and visual-script graphs: framework, compile/validation contract, debugging, diff and merge.\ncollaboration-version-control :: Source-control integration, locking and checkout, multi-user concurrent editing, merge tooling for scene and asset data, content review, large-binary storage strategy.\nai-assisted-authoring :: Evaluates and integrates AI-assisted authoring: generative asset tools, editor copilots, ML-assisted retopology/rigging/UV/LOD, provenance and licensing of generated content.\nbuild-system-toolchains :: Build graph, compiler and toolchain matrix, C++ modules/unity/PCH, compile caching and distribution, codegen integration, third-party dependencies, static analysis, build configurations.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9bcf4c40-6e86-4532-8050-046ee0ff7979","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:50:04.000Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"191240bb-daa2-4fe5-be59-85dcd3d81293","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
